  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Syria: reconstruction after the earthquake</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to support the recovery of people and the reconstruction of houses and buildings that where severely damaged by the massive 7.8 magnitudo earthquake that rocked Turkey and Northern Syria. The reconstruction activities will be carried out in Aleppo, Latakia and other cities in Syria. The earthquake and its following tremors took more than 50,000 lives and caused an estimated $5.1 billion in damages. The impact in Syria has been exacerbated by the ongoing decade-long conflict.</narrative>
  </description>
